Z||000021||Jaygee79||09-16-2001||10:50 PM||||I couldn't find any flags anywhere.  So I printed out a picture of one, laminated it, and put it on my antenna.  Only problem is if I drive over 30mph it flaps like crazy and makes my antenna fly back and forth.  It was at the top at first, but I moved it halfway down both to fix that and to have it at half-staff.  Let's see if that's better.<P>My grandfather gave me a flag, but it only had 48 stars on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>hey, why isn't my sig working?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ranger Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg[/IMG][img]http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Formula88||09-17-2001||01:10 AM||||Manufacturer's can't keep up with the demand on flags.  But more are coming - keep looking.  Most craft stores, A.C. Moore, Michaels, etc. should be getting more in.  As for the raising prices, well, just don't do business with them.  Any reputable company will not raise prices at this time.  The know they'll make a killing anyway due to extra demand.  Hiking the prices is just an insult.<P>You might check out <A HREF="http://www.allflags.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.allflags.com</A>  . They are pledging to not raise their prices during this time, and that they are taking orders and will ship them as quick as inventory is available.||||reg||1
Z||000023||stsmithgt||09-17-2001||10:52 AM||||Thanks Rick  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Oh man, even with the super glue on the seams, it still is trying to shread a little on the ends of the stripes.  I guess it wasn't made for "freeway" speeds.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Once I can find more flags that are better than the .50¢ plastic ones they have left at this time, I'll try  pressing in a thin coat of 100% silicone next time  to get more flexability.  Hopefully that won't make the colors run.<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
